{
  "id": 22,
  "name": "spread_density_gated_regret_v2",
  "intent": "Augment parent's spread-only regret gate with a cluster_density modulation so regret is amplified inside genuine clusters (where uniqueness is real) and dampened in uniform/sparse fields where the signal is noisy. Add a bounded early-phase mean_remaining penalty to discourage picks to peripheral nodes far from the unvisited centroid, addressing uniform-case underperformance where simple NN drifts via scattered detours. Keep the quadratic return ramp and nearest_remaining term as anchors. Hypothesis: combining density-aware regret with a centroid-pull in the first half should tighten tour quality on uniform instances without regressing clustered/grid cases.",
  "tags": [
    "cluster",
    "nonlinear"
  ],
  "code": "def priority(f):\n    p = f['progress']\n    s = f['spread']\n    cd = f['cluster_density']\n    rw = 0.15 + 0.4*p + 0.3*p*p\n    rel = s / (0.4 + s + 1e-9)\n    rgw = (0.05 + 0.15*p) * (0.3 + 0.7*rel) * (0.6 + 0.4*cd)\n    return -f['distance'] + rw*f['return_distance'] + rgw*f['regret'] + 0.05*f['nearest_remaining'] - 0.1*(1-p)*f['mean_remaining']",
  "source": "live_llm",
  "parent_id": 17,
  "reference_id": null,
